# === PowerLine Challenge (PLC) monorepo ===

# Dependencies (dev-only tooling under cartridges; never deployed)
node_modules/

# OS / editor / OneDrive cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
*.tmp

# Oversized uncompressed source audio — GitHub rejects any file over 100MB.
# POLICY: compress before committing. Web Audio decodeAudioData handles OGG/MP3/Opus/
# FLAC natively, and the loaders build URLs by filename, so the container is a free
# choice — no code change is needed to swap a stem's format.
# Resolved 2026-09-08: Background1.wav (241 MiB, 32-bit float, 11:56) was the only
# entry here. It is now files/music/Background1.ogg (8.9 MiB, OGG Vorbis, byte-for-byte
# the same 31,588,605 frames), wired as the menu bed and COMMITTED, so this rule had
# nothing left to ignore.
# Deliberately NOT replaced with a blanket *.wav rule: the SFX library is WAV-based
# and 12 stems are tracked, so a wildcard would silently hide legitimate new ones.
# Add a specific path here if another oversized master ever lands.

# === C64 disk library (Game/disks/) ==========================================
# 🚨 THIS REPO IS PUBLIC AND HAS NO PRE-PUSH HOOK. Disk images committed here
# would be published to github.com and to GitHub Pages, permanently — deleting
# them later does not undo it. The folder is user-curated on each machine and
# travels EMPTY on purpose; an empty library is a normal state the hub handles.
# 🚫 Do not un-ignore this. See Game/disks/README.md.
Game/disks/*
!Game/disks/README.md

# === Disk artwork (Game/cat/assets/disk-art/) ================================
# Same rule, same reason, added 2026-09-12: sleeve scans and box art of
# commercial games are other people's artwork, and this repo is public. The
# hub finds images by listing the folder, so it travels with only its README.
# 🚫 Do not un-ignore this. See Game/cat/assets/disk-art/README.md.
Game/cat/assets/disk-art/*
!Game/cat/assets/disk-art/README.md

# === The real-C64 rig's screenshot (Game/cat/verify-c64-run.png) ==============
# Same reason again, added 2026-09-17. verify-c64.mjs RUNs a disk from the
# library above and photographs the result for a human eye: the first run caught
# a commercial game's box art in the preview frame and a crack group's trainer
# screen on the C64. The rig rewrites it every run, so it stays on disk and out
# of git. (verify-cat-*.png are tracked: they show the hub with no game running.)
Game/cat/verify-c64-run.png

# EmulatorJS self-hosted core data (Game/cat/emulator/data/).
# Third-party GPL build artefacts, ~10-15MB, fetched per-machine rather than
# vendored — see Game/cat/emulator/README.md for the one command that gets it.
Game/cat/emulator/data/

# === Raw CAD exports and working copies in cartridge dataset folders ==========
# 🚨 THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. A CAD export dropped into a datasets folder carries a
# CALL IDENTIFIER IN ITS FILENAME, and a filename is published as surely as the
# bytes are. One had been sitting untracked in Asteroid Command's datasets
# folder ("Shorthand Comments-MXl3514410-TR.csv", found 2026-09-12); it was NOT
# ignored, so any broad `git add` would have staged it and the next push would
# have put that number on github.com permanently.
#
# 🚫 AND IT IS NOT `files/datasets/`, WHICH IS THE OBVIOUS RULE AND THE WRONG
# ONE. Measured before writing this: that folder is ALREADY TRACKED AND PUBLIC —
# 10 files under Asteroid Command alone (bases.csv, commands.csv, scoring.csv,
# the master .xlsx, and the curated `Shorthand Comments.csv`), plus Pitstop's and
# The Aquanaut's. .gitignore does not untrack what is already tracked, so a
# blanket rule there would not remove anything; it would simply be A RULE THAT
# LIES — claiming datasets are ignored while ten of them are committed beside it,
# and making the next legitimate dataset need a `-f` nobody expects.
# ⚠️ `core.ignoreCase` is TRUE on this machine, so a bare `datasets/` would also
# have matched `Archive/Cartridges/.../Datasets/`, which is public on purpose.
#
# ⭐ So these are narrow and were each checked against `git ls-files` first:
# neither matches anything currently tracked.
#   *-TR.csv  the CAD export suffix, which is where the identifier rides
#   *.bak     Excel/editor working copies, never source
# 📌 The curated dataset a cartridge actually LOADS keeps its plain name and
# stays tracked. If you add a dataset and git refuses it, check the name against
# these two patterns before reaching for `git add -f`.
*-TR.csv
*.bak
